		{
			"to": "western-civ/hammurabi",
			"why": "The Covenant Code of Exodus 21–23 rules on the same cases as Hammurabi's laws 117 to 252, the debt slave, the eye put out and the goring ox, in the same if-then form, but with different penalties."
		},
		{
			"to": "western-civ/gutenberg-bible",
			"why": "The Gutenberg Bible printed Jerome's Latin Vulgate, whose Old Testament Jerome translated from the Hebrew Bible rather than from the Greek Septuagint."
		},
		{
			"to": "chemistry/iron-gall-ink",
			"why": "The Dead Sea Scrolls are written in carbon ink made from lamp soot, the older ink that iron gall ink later displaced in Europe's manuscripts."
